// A long double is not a word, so an operation on one hands crt/ldbl the address
// of a 16-byte frame temporary for the result (ld_tmp makes one per use, its slot
// grown into the frame now: the frame is final only once the function's blocks
// are printed) and the addresses of the operands, and the call's value is that
// address. An arithmetic operator answers the temporary; a comparison answers
// cld_cmp's 0 or 1 for the operator's code (the position in fl_ops after the
// four arithmetic ones: < 0, <= 1, > 2, >= 3, == 4, != 5).
ld_tmp() {
  int t = new_temp(ty_ldbl());
  int a = newleaf("un", t, 0, "&", "");
  string s = ex_txt(a);
} return string s;
